WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.935
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.303
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.772
between Wendy's in the UK and the US.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.407
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:14.714
In the UK, Wendy's iconic
Frosties come in three sizes,

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.250
junior, regular, and large.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.819
In the US, we actually
have four Frosty sizes,

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.956
junior, small, medium, large.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.592
We're going to pour out the largest Frosty

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.527
to see how big it is compared to the US's.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.531
The classic hamburger at a Wendy's

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.699
is called a Dave's,

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.601
named after the founder, Dave Thomas.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:37.303
Ours come in singles,
doubles, and triples.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.605
Our burgers are the same in the UK.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:41.041
They also come as singles,
doubles, or triples.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.810
Joe: Now we're going to weigh a US triple.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.180
Pretty close. 14 ounces for our triple.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.848
Now, while a triple might
be the official limit

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.050
on burger sizes at Wendy's,

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.251
Wendy's enthusiasts have come up

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.219
with something called a Meat Cube.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.554
This is a secret menu item

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.556
where you actually take
an extra meat patty

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.457
and add it to this,

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.792
so you get four patties,

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.360
which I think adds up to around a pound.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.895
Joe, I'm officially challenging you

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.196
to a Meat Cube showdown.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.698
The fastest person to eat
the entire Meat Cube wins.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:06.299
You think you got it?

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.134
I accept your challenge, Harry.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.506
Let's do this.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:16.142
Harry: Three, two, one.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.177
Joe: Start.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.189
This is a lot of beef.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.391
I see why the triple is the limit now.

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:32.225
Time?

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.293
Conner: 1:07.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.594
I wish I had more time to chew it.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:39.933
[coughing]

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.704
Need the sauce. Need some moisture.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.474
[grunts]

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.109
The buns!

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.046
Harry: Oh, God.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.648
[Joe stammering]

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.084
Joe: How'd I do?

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.719
Harry: Done.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.990
Yeah!

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.358
Woo!

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.626
USA, baby!

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.460
Conner: How do you feel?

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.728
Oh, terrible.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.763
I feel absolutely terrible. [coughs]

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.866
And yet elated that I won.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:15.702
Well, now we know why the US
has such an obesity problem.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.505
OK. That's quite enough of that.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.707
Back to our regularly
scheduled programming.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.543
Another iconic Wendy's
menu item is the Baconator.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.745
In the UK, these just come
in one size, as a regular.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.714
Of course, in the US we
also have the Baconator,

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:30.083
but we have a smaller Baconator

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.519
known as the Son of Baconator.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.854
Something incredibly unsettling about

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.790
a burger having a child
that's also a burger.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.560
This Baconator giving
birth to that Baconator.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.494
Harry: And, of course,
we're going to weigh

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.796
the regular Baconators
to see whose is bigger.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.532
The highly regarded Wendy's nuggets

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:48.134
that come in regular or
spicy. Love the spicy.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:52.405
They come in units of four, six, and 10.

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.407
Nuggets in the UK only
come in two portion sizes,

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.675
four and eight.

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.913
Wendy's, of course, has fries,

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:02.115
and those fries in the
US come in four sizes,

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:04.817
junior, small, medium, large.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.486
Our fries also come in four sizes,

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.855
value, small, medium, and large.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:11.191
Let's weigh our large fries
to see who's getting more.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:14.027
Ours is way less.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.497
Hmm.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:18.831
What's that all about?

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:22.101
Another side that is
probably unique to Wendy's,

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.304
I can't think of any other
fast-food place that does this,

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.272
is Wendy's chili.

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:30.643
It has been on the menu
since it opened back in 1969.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:33.012
In the US, you can get your chili,

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:35.048
ugh, for whatever reason,

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:37.517
in two sizes, small and large.

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.185
In the UK, we only have one size of chili,

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:39.986
which is this one.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.287
We're going to weigh it
against the largest size

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:43.223
in the US to find the difference.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.657
Finally, let's compare drinks.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.726
In the US, you can get
three sizes of drink,

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.394
small, medium, and large.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.797
On the internet, it does not specify

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:53.800
how much fluid ounces are in any of these.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.769
If I had to guess, too much; way too much;

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:57.604
way, way too much.

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:59.405
In the UK, drinks come in three sizes,

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.241
small, medium, or large.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.375
And these are advertised as being

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:05.445
12, 16, and 20 ounces, respectively.

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:06.646
Let's measure the largest drinks

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:07.914
to see which country's is bigger.

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.753
So, our large drink
actually came out as closer

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.755
to 18 ounces than closer to 20.

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:16.723
I will say that in the UK

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.590
you fill up your own drink,

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.192
so maybe I just needed to fill a bit more.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.960
OK, so their large is 18 ounces.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.794
What is our small?

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.899
20 ounces. So our small is
bigger than their large.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.235
Man, we love drinking our
calories in this country.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.671
We love drinking our calories.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:33.906
For this episode, we
thought it might be fun

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:36.509
to compare some prices from
Wendy's in the UK and the US.

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:38.911
Let's use this Baconator
as a basis for comparison.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.781
In the US, a Baconator
on its own, no combo,

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:44.117
would cost $7.39.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.451
The same burger in the UK will cost you

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.887
£6.29, which, at the
time of recording this,

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:51.090
was around $8.90, which is a 20% increase.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.559
However, if you were to turn
this into a medium combo,

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.561
yes, this is the medium,

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.097
the price would go up to $11.19.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.466
Whereas in the UK, adding
a Baconator to a combo meal

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:03.002
will only increase the price to £7.09.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.605
So, actually, a US meal
is now 11% more expensive.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.874
Whoa, whoa, whoa, Harry,
don't get ahead of yourself.

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:10.443
Wendy's in the US has
an ace up its sleeve,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.245
the 4 for $4 promotion. 

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:12.979
[clears throat]

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:15.081
You can get your choice of
a junior bacon cheeseburger;

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.083
a junior cheeseburger, seen here;

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.252
a double stack; or a
crispy chicken sandwich

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.554
along with junior fries, four nuggets,

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:24.657
and a value drink. All of this, 4 bucks.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.392
Sadly, Wendy's has not
replicated that deal

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.960
here in the UK, not even in the form

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.662
of a 4 for £4 deal.

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.030
If you were to buy all the components

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.366
of a US 4 for $4 here in the UK,

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:36.636
it would cost you £6.36,
which is about $9.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.305
That's a 125% increase on the US price.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.907
The real damage here
is done by the nuggets,

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:43.476
which cost £2.99 on their own in the UK.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.511
That's around $4.24,

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.214
aka more than the entire
4 for $4 combo in the US.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.183
So it looks like the
US provides more value

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:52.018
if you're a little smart
about what you order

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.119
and how you order it.

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:56.322
Say you walk into a US Wendy's

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.358
and you want to get the
Baconator combo meal.

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:01.327
Just how unhealthy is it, you ask?

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.829
Well, I will tell you. OK.

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:04.997
The burger, 960 calories.

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:07.266
Fries, 360 calories.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.402
And the drink, medium, right? Coke, OK,

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:11.437
it's going to be 370 calories.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:14.440
This whole shebang, 1,690 calories.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.843
That's 84% of your daily allowance.

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:18.845
What about the same meal here in the UK?

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:20.713
Well, our Baconator is
actually more calorific,

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:23.049
as it comes in at 1,010 calories.

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.485
However, the fries are just 239 calories,

00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:26.853
and the Coke, just 200,

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:29.856
leaving the total at 1,449.

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:32.191
That's a 16% decrease from the US.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.227
What, you ask, is the most calorific thing

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:35.428
on the Wendy's US menu?

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:37.263
It is this burger in front of me.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:39.999
The pretzel bacon pub triple.

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:41.000
Look at this thing.

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:43.369
Goodness.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:46.339
1,520 calories.

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:49.942
106 grams of fat. 45 of
those grams are saturated.

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:53.746
That's 135% of your daily fat allowance.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:55.948
Sadly, that's a US exclusive,
and our most calorific item

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.617
is actually just the Dave's triple.

00:06:57.617 --> 00:07:00.887
In the UK, one of these is 1,204 calories,

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:04.056
with 81 grams of fat, of
which 33 grams are saturated.

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:09.262
Thankfully, Wendy's discloses
a full ingredients list

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.830
for both the UK and the US,

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:11.831
so let's take a closer look

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:13.833
at some of the menu items right now.

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:16.235
Here is everything that's in
a Wendy's Baconator in the UK.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.571
Strap in, because this is
a long ingredients section.

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:22.308
Premium bun. Wheat flour,
water, sugar, yeast.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:25.778
Mayonnaise. Rapeseed oil (78%), water.

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:28.481
Ketchup. Tomatoes, 148 grams.

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:31.818
American cheese slice.
Cheese (70%) (milk).

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:33.386
Beef patty. 100% beef.

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:35.488
Bacon. Sugar, water.

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:39.659
Table salt. Salt, anticaking
agent, sodium ferrocyanide.

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:40.960
Seems like a lot, right?

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.195
Well, guess what?

00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:43.596
We got the UK beat again.

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:46.232
Here's everything in a US Baconator.

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:47.266
Start with the premium bun.

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:48.734
Enriched flour, which is wheat flour,

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:51.170
malted barley flour, niacin, reduced iron,

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:56.142
[fast-forwarding]

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:58.544
sodium nitrite. [exhales]

00:07:58.544 --> 00:07:59.412
That's all of it.

00:07:59.412 --> 00:08:00.847
Whew. Now, that is a long list.

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:01.681
And is there anything in there

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:02.815
that you should be worried about?

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:04.450
Well, we can start with sodium nitrite,

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:06.586
which is found in the
applewood-smoked bacon.

00:08:06.586 --> 00:08:09.188
Sodium nitrite is a
chemical used to cure meats,

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:11.491
and it gives them that
appealing pink color,

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:12.859
which is perfect for bacon.

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:14.193
It's also super toxic.

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:16.562
It's prohibited for sale on
certain websites, like eBay,

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.331
because it's been used
in homicide attempts,

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:19.765
and a dental assistant once died

00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:22.168
after eating just a
1-gram tablet by mistake.

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:23.603
Thankfully, there's
none of that in the UK,

00:08:23.603 --> 00:08:24.437
but just like the US,

00:08:24.437 --> 00:08:26.439
we do have lecithin in
our American cheese.

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:27.540
According to some academics,

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.309
there are a "worrisome
number" of scientific studies

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:32.445
which have suggested that
it can promote depression,

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:33.880
which is kind of the
last thing that I need.

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.183
Outside of the Baconator,

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:39.051
there are one or two ingredients
you should watch out for

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:41.554
in the pretzel bacon pub burger.

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:43.723
The pretzel bun contains
potassium chloride,

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:45.758
which in normal food doses is fine,

00:08:45.758 --> 00:08:47.460
but is one of the three ingredients

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:50.563
in the three-drug cocktail
used for lethal injection.

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:52.131
Apparently, enough of it would cause

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:54.333
an abnormal heartbeat and cardiac arrest.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:55.201
Let's be honest.

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:57.169
If anything in this burger
is stopping your heart,

00:08:57.169 --> 00:08:58.938
it's gonna be the
cholesterol and saturated fat

00:08:58.938 --> 00:09:00.506
long before the potassium chloride.

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:03.142
The pickles also contain polysorbate 80.

00:09:03.142 --> 00:09:05.444
Now, this is commonly used as
an emulsifier in some foods,

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:07.480
but with pickles it's
used as a solubilizer,

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.881
which means that it
helps other ingredients

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:09.916
dissolve in the brine.

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:12.585
The bad news is studies have suggested

00:09:12.585 --> 00:09:15.888
that it can cause colon
cancer in mice. Yikes.

00:09:17.857 --> 00:09:19.625
Here's everything you'll
find at a Wendy's in the UK

00:09:19.625 --> 00:09:20.893
that you won't find in the US.

00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:24.063
And here is everything you
can get at a US Wendy's

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.364
you can't get in the UK.

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:28.968
This is ridiculous. [laughs]

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:30.369
Let's start with the burgers.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:31.203
Now, as far as I can tell,

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:33.139
we only have three exclusive burgers,

00:09:33.139 --> 00:09:35.341
one of which I'm not even
sure is an exclusive burger,

00:09:35.341 --> 00:09:37.543
which is this one, the
cheeseburger deluxe.

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:39.345
The reason I'm not sure
if it's an exclusive

00:09:39.345 --> 00:09:41.047
is because in the US you
guys have something called

00:09:41.047 --> 00:09:42.481
a junior cheeseburger deluxe,

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:44.283
which looked very similar to this.

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:45.952
And I just wanted to check if

00:09:45.952 --> 00:09:47.353
what you guys consider junior

00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:49.155
we consider deluxe over here.

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:50.723
Yes, Harry, they look pretty similar.

00:09:50.723 --> 00:09:52.491
The only difference I could find is that

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:55.928
ours has ketchup and mayo
and yours has "sauce."

00:09:55.928 --> 00:09:58.130
So I guess it boils down
to whatever your sauce is.

00:09:58.164 --> 00:10:00.633
Next up we've got this one,
which is the Veggie Stack.

00:10:00.633 --> 00:10:02.034
It's a vegetarian exclusive.

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:04.637
There's definitely some,
like, corn in there.

00:10:04.637 --> 00:10:06.872
Some kind of, like, black
bean, kidney bean thing,

00:10:06.872 --> 00:10:08.474
maybe some carrot and pepper.

00:10:14.547 --> 00:10:17.049
It's not for me, but I
am a die-hard carnivore,

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:19.051
so maybe there's vegetarians out there

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:20.119
who'll appreciate this a lot more.

00:10:20.119 --> 00:10:21.821
Our final exclusive sandwich is this one,

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:23.322
the avocado chicken club.

00:10:23.322 --> 00:10:26.292
Oh, my goodness. We have
so much to go through.

00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:29.428
I guess I will start with the burgers.

00:10:31.364 --> 00:10:35.034
Here is something called the
bourbon bacon cheeseburger.

00:10:35.034 --> 00:10:36.802
And we have bourbon barbecue sauce.

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:39.405
Something for Wendy's burger aficionados.

00:10:39.405 --> 00:10:42.308
The pretzel bacon pub cheeseburger.

00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:44.210
I think it comes in one,
two, or three stacks.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.911
This is the three stacker.

00:10:45.911 --> 00:10:48.180
OK. The double stack,

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:50.916
which is two patties, cheese, bacon.

00:10:50.916 --> 00:10:52.284
A junior hamburger.

00:10:52.284 --> 00:10:55.888
Junior hamburger. Look how
small this is. For the kids.

00:10:55.888 --> 00:10:58.991
Junior cheeseburger deluxe. Ooh, yeah.

00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:01.761
Lettuce, onion, tomato, pickles.

00:11:01.761 --> 00:11:02.595
There it is.

00:11:02.595 --> 00:11:05.865
The Big Bacon Classic.

00:11:05.865 --> 00:11:08.100
OK. So they went to
the chicken. All right.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.769
Chicken goodies.

00:11:09.769 --> 00:11:13.706
The Asiago ranch chicken sandwich.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:18.644
OK, this is the jalapeño popper sandwich.

00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:21.280
The pretzel bun bacon pub sandwich.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.749
Crispy chicken BLT sandwich.

00:11:23.749 --> 00:11:25.651
It looks to be what a BLT would be

00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:28.287
with a little chicken guy in there.

00:11:28.587 --> 00:11:29.455
[sighs]

00:11:29.455 --> 00:11:31.891
So, spicy nuggets. I mentioned before.

00:11:31.891 --> 00:11:34.360
The spicy is way better than the regulars.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:34.994
Way better.

00:11:35.194 --> 00:11:36.028
Then we have a couple of

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:37.396
exclusive salad options in the UK.

00:11:37.396 --> 00:11:39.432
I'm usually pretty suspicious
of fast-food salads,

00:11:39.432 --> 00:11:41.067
but I've got to say, these
actually do look pretty good.

00:11:41.133 --> 00:11:42.735
The first exclusive salad
that I wanted to show you

00:11:42.735 --> 00:11:44.270
was the avocado veggie salad.

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:45.638
However, I think they
got the order mixed up

00:11:45.638 --> 00:11:48.207
and gave me an avocado
chicken salad instead.

00:11:48.207 --> 00:11:50.309
So what I was supposed
to get was this salad,

00:11:50.309 --> 00:11:51.977
which contains avocado,

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:53.379
and then instead of the chicken and bacon,

00:11:53.379 --> 00:11:55.514
we're supposed to get
some of the veggie bites,

00:11:55.514 --> 00:11:56.682
but mixed up in there instead.

00:11:56.682 --> 00:11:58.851
And then the second
exclusive salad is this one.

00:11:58.851 --> 00:12:00.920
This is the apple cranberry chicken salad.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.488
You know it's a good
salad when they give you

00:12:02.488 --> 00:12:05.624
the dressing and some other
accoutrement on the side

00:12:05.624 --> 00:12:06.926
instead of just jumbling it all up

00:12:06.926 --> 00:12:08.060
and then, like, letting it get soggy.

00:12:08.294 --> 00:12:09.895
We got four salads.

00:12:09.895 --> 00:12:11.397
Man, jalapeño popper again.

00:12:11.397 --> 00:12:14.133
The chicken, the bacon, jalapeños, cheese.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:15.801
Taco salad.

00:12:15.801 --> 00:12:17.236
Hey, is there any...?

00:12:18.337 --> 00:12:19.271
There's no ground beef on this.

00:12:19.271 --> 00:12:20.106
There's no meat on this.

00:12:20.406 --> 00:12:22.308
It's like what you would
put on tacos at home.

00:12:22.308 --> 00:12:25.177
Shredded cheese, shredded
lettuce, cut-up tomatoes.

00:12:25.177 --> 00:12:26.545
Next salad!

00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:28.681
Apple pecan salad.

00:12:28.681 --> 00:12:30.750
The summer strawberry salad.

00:12:31.217 --> 00:12:32.251
[grunts]

00:12:33.319 --> 00:12:36.622
Chicken, bacon, strawberries. Yeah, OK.

00:12:36.722 --> 00:12:38.357
We have one other exclusive veggie option,

00:12:38.357 --> 00:12:39.959
which is this one.

00:12:39.959 --> 00:12:41.894
These are veggie bites.

00:12:41.894 --> 00:12:43.529
Now, these are a vegetarian alternative

00:12:43.529 --> 00:12:45.131
to Wendy's chicken nuggets.

00:12:45.131 --> 00:12:48.134
Just judging from kind of
the look and smell of them,

00:12:48.134 --> 00:12:49.335
I think they're made from probably

00:12:49.335 --> 00:12:52.705
a very similar blend to
the Veggie Stack burger.

00:12:53.873 --> 00:12:56.008
And for that reason, I
probably won't try and eat one.

00:12:56.008 --> 00:12:59.044
It looks like falafel but just
smells and feels way worse.

00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:00.546
[laughs]

00:13:00.546 --> 00:13:03.149
I love falafel, and I don't love these.

00:13:04.016 --> 00:13:06.285
The pub fries. Yes.

00:13:06.285 --> 00:13:09.789
Who hasn't been in a pub
getting a pint with the lads?

00:13:09.789 --> 00:13:10.990
Man, they're really pushing strawberries

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:12.625
this summer, Wendy's.

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:14.293
And the salad? And then they got these?

00:13:14.293 --> 00:13:15.761
Two things equals a lot to me.

00:13:15.761 --> 00:13:17.763
Also got a thing of apple slices.

00:13:17.763 --> 00:13:20.299
I don't know if this is a solo side.

00:13:20.299 --> 00:13:21.534
I don't know why we have apple slices.

00:13:21.534 --> 00:13:23.068
If you need something
to dip your veggie bites

00:13:23.068 --> 00:13:24.003
or anything else into,

00:13:24.003 --> 00:13:26.372
then we have a couple of
exclusive sauce options as well.

00:13:26.438 --> 00:13:28.007
Deep voice: Sauce talk.

00:13:28.007 --> 00:13:30.409
Harry: We'll start with this
one, which is a garlic mayo.

00:13:30.409 --> 00:13:32.344
And then our other
exclusive sauce is this one,

00:13:32.344 --> 00:13:34.246
which is a pot of Heinz sweet chili.

00:13:34.246 --> 00:13:35.981
We love sweet chili sauce here in the UK.

00:13:35.981 --> 00:13:37.349
I don't know why, but it's just offered

00:13:37.349 --> 00:13:39.151
by a lot of big fast-food chains.

00:13:39.218 --> 00:13:40.953
I got a whole bag here.

00:13:41.987 --> 00:13:43.255
Dipping sauces.

00:13:43.255 --> 00:13:45.057
Buttermilk ranch.

00:13:45.057 --> 00:13:47.293
Ooh, creamy sriracha.

00:13:48.093 --> 00:13:49.862
Side of S'Awesome.

00:13:50.029 --> 00:13:54.166
Something called the hot chili seasoning.

00:13:54.266 --> 00:13:55.935
We also have a few
exclusive breakfast items

00:13:55.935 --> 00:13:57.736
from the UK Wendy's,
starting with this one,

00:13:57.736 --> 00:13:59.738
which is just an egg and
cheese breakfast sandwich.

00:13:59.738 --> 00:14:00.973
I'm sure they would make you one of these

00:14:00.973 --> 00:14:01.874
in the US if you asked,

00:14:01.874 --> 00:14:03.943
but it's actually a default
menu item in the UK,

00:14:03.943 --> 00:14:06.011
whereas it didn't look
like it was one in the US.

00:14:06.011 --> 00:14:07.046
And true to form for the UK,

00:14:07.046 --> 00:14:09.215
we have three different
porridge options for breakfast.

00:14:09.348 --> 00:14:10.950
We have plain porridge.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.017
Add some jam to it.

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:13.419
They give you a little sachet of jam,

00:14:13.419 --> 00:14:15.120
and you squeeze that into your porridge.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.222
And, finally, probably the most

00:14:16.222 --> 00:14:17.890
exciting porridge option,
which is this one.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.658
It's the cranberry seed porridge.

00:14:19.892 --> 00:14:22.728
There's a lot of breakfast
sandwiches to go through,

00:14:22.728 --> 00:14:24.430
so let's give it a shot.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:25.631
I'll just go down the line here.

00:14:25.631 --> 00:14:29.134
Maple bacon chicken croissant sandwich.

00:14:29.134 --> 00:14:31.270
Everything square with Wendy's.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.938
Sausage, egg, and cheese biscuit.

00:14:32.938 --> 00:14:33.839
[grunts]

00:14:33.839 --> 00:14:35.941
Bacon, egg, and cheese biscuit.

00:14:36.942 --> 00:14:37.776
Sausage biscuit.

00:14:37.776 --> 00:14:39.411
Yeah, these are always, like,

00:14:39.411 --> 00:14:40.579
it's just, it really is

00:14:40.579 --> 00:14:42.848
just the sausage patty and a biscuit.

00:14:42.848 --> 00:14:45.317
Like, can you think of something drier

00:14:45.317 --> 00:14:46.218
to have in the morning?

00:14:46.218 --> 00:14:48.487
Breakfast burrito. This thing is ice cold.

00:14:48.487 --> 00:14:49.788
I'm sorry, Wendy's.

00:14:49.788 --> 00:14:52.791
I did not mean to misrepresent
your breakfast burrito.

00:14:52.791 --> 00:14:54.159
I'm sure it's great.

00:14:54.159 --> 00:14:57.162
This thing, it's like, jeez, Louise.

00:14:57.162 --> 00:14:59.899
Oh, no, I don't even know
what this is. Conner!

00:14:59.899 --> 00:15:01.700
Chicken biscuit.

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:04.436
Biscuit and fried
chicken. And nothing else.

00:15:05.971 --> 00:15:08.240
The Wendy's in the US, you can
get a cold brew iced coffee,

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:12.578
a vanilla Frosty-ccino, and
a chocolate Frosty-ccino.

00:15:12.645 --> 00:15:14.480
Now, we have a few
exclusive drinks in the UK,

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:15.948
but they're pretty much all hot drinks.

00:15:15.948 --> 00:15:17.650
Now, it looked like in
the US you guys can get

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:19.451
the very basic kind of filter coffee

00:15:19.451 --> 00:15:22.021
or you can get the Frosty-ccinos
and stuff like that,

00:15:22.021 --> 00:15:24.523
whereas in the UK, we have a
whole range of espresso drinks.

00:15:24.523 --> 00:15:26.625
You can get things like
lattes and cappuccinos,

00:15:26.625 --> 00:15:28.193
as well as some breakfast teas.

00:15:28.327 --> 00:15:30.996
They have a bunch of lemonades.

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:32.431
One has an N on it.

00:15:32.431 --> 00:15:34.166
Is this the all-natural lemonade?

00:15:34.166 --> 00:15:36.201
It is. Wow. And this
lemonade's really good.

00:15:36.201 --> 00:15:38.203
Strawberry lemonade is excellent. Man.

00:15:38.203 --> 00:15:39.772
Wendy's with the strawberries this year.

00:15:39.772 --> 00:15:41.407
Pineapple mango.

00:15:44.076 --> 00:15:45.344
Ooh, yeah.

00:15:45.344 --> 00:15:47.780
Tropical, kind of. Tropical.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.348
I bet it's tropical berry!

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.651
Good drinks.

00:15:52.651 --> 00:15:55.154
Now, also, I'm looking for
a Flashin' Fruit Punch,

00:15:55.154 --> 00:15:58.090
an iced tea, and a sweet iced tea.

00:15:58.090 --> 00:15:59.158
And for desserts at Wendy's,

00:15:59.158 --> 00:16:00.326
you can get yourself an oatmeal bar,

00:16:01.493 --> 00:16:03.128
chocolate chunk cookie,

00:16:04.229 --> 00:16:06.598
and, last but not least,

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.501
sugar cookie.

00:16:09.501 --> 00:16:13.572
That, ladies and gentlemen, is it!

00:16:13.572 --> 00:16:15.541
We're done. Cut.

00:16:15.541 --> 00:16:17.943
Dude, it would be so funny

00:16:17.943 --> 00:16:19.545
if I threw up in the middle of this.

00:16:19.545 --> 00:16:20.913
If I have to puke, I'm
not gonna say anything.

00:16:20.913 --> 00:16:22.614
I'm just gonna barf right on the desk.

00:16:23.549 --> 00:16:25.184
I'm not putting that shirt
back on. I'm too hot.

00:16:25.184 --> 00:16:26.618
Ugh. [burps]

